<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23782" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sēmĭno</span></b> , 1,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to sow</i> or <i>plant in</i>, <i>to implant</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tabem et morbos visceribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					19, 5, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra ex caelestium imbrium conceptionibus
					inseminata,</span>”
				<i>impregnated</i>, <i>fertilized</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8 praef.</span></i>
			
			<i>init.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex conventu Jovis inseminati et nati sunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 93</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 17, 35</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">68</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
